The current production checklist requires evaluating a model change on a frozen holdout before promotion. The release policy mandates that models can only be promoted if F1 improves by at least 0.005 and ROC-AUC does not drop by more than 0.01. A drift alert alone does not authorize promotion. The legacy memo, which was superseded by the release policy, allowed promoting any model when accuracy exceeded 0.80 without requiring a frozen holdout evaluation.

Therefore, the owner cannot ignore the frozen holdout because the legacy memo's process is superseded by the current release policy. The owner must follow the updated guidelines to ensure model quality and stability.

